{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unaroused-destitute-cobra","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Observation (read-only, 2026-11-18 PST)\nThe operator's model (decision on `placid-dreary-zethuswasp`, 2026-11-18): each environment has its own signing key; checkouts in the same environment may share one. The live store does not match that model for one key.\n\n- The authorship key with SHA-256 fingerprint prefix `oGCqzgfDMp` (public-key comment `rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907`) signs events under 2 environment ids:\n  - `ad49f17f-…`: the review bot's tickets clone (`/var/gerrit/site/reviewbot-tickets/.env-id`, per the read-only evidence in `placid-dreary-zethuswasp`'s description). 980 live events signed with it, author \"Rebar Bot\", 2026-09-07 18:05 to 2026-11-18 21:05 PST.\n  - `492a5c71-…`: the operator's Mac checkout (`/Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.tickets-tracker/.env-id`). 509 live events, author \"Rebar Bot Nava\", 2026-11-04 to 2026-11-16 PST (1,338 including compacted events, from 2026-11-02 13:20).\n- The Mac's configured `identity.signing_key` is `~/.config/rebar/rebar-bot-signing-key`, file time 2026-11-02 13:18 PST. Its public half has fingerprint prefix `oGCqzgfDMp`, the same key.\n- Before 2026-09-07, every environment (Mac clones, review bot, MCP server's predecessor, bridge, reconciler) signed with the earlier key `PU4nHIqJCR`. The MCP server (`eea68b7f`) moved to its own keys (`YWib9Gj1qZ` until 2026-09-07, `biqEFL9T96` from 2026-09-15).\n\nSo the same private key lives in at least 2 environments: the server's review-bot clone and the Mac.\n\n## Consequence\nUnder the key-based `ENV_ID_MISMATCH` rule, env ids signed by one key are treated as checkouts of one environment. A `.env-id` carried between the review bot and the Mac would not be reported. Signatures from that key cannot tell the two writers apart.\n\n## Not done here\nNo key was changed, revoked or rotated, and no deployment was changed. Choosing which environment gets a new key, and whether to revoke this one, is an operator decision.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The review bot's clone and the Mac sign with different authorship keys: operator records each environment's public-key fingerprint and the date of the change in a ticket comment.\n  provenance: environment=rebar production host and operator Mac; principal=operator; privilege_posture=key administration; instrument=ssh-keygen -lf on each environment's configured identity.signing_key — key placement is an operator decision outside the codebase.","id":"9c9a-3331-822f-401c","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":["ops-sweep"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"The review bot's tickets clone and the operator's Mac sign events with the same authorship key"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1795067860946112749,"uuid":"8bffef09-b206-4df9-b1f7-fbad2c4186a7"}